{
  "rationale": "The plant automata G model the robot's perception (obstacle sensors) and motion capabilities (open-loop pulses for each action). The specification automata E enforce conservative exploration: random_walk is used for exploration in clear states, move_forward is only allowed in a dedicated commit state, and all obstacle events force deterministic turn-based recovery before returning to exploration. No random_walk or move_forward is allowed in obstacle recovery states. All uncontrollable events are handled in every state, and only one controllable is enabled per non-terminal state.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception and motion to reflect the robot's hardware and sensing/motion decoupling.",
    "Specification automata bind sensor outcomes to safe actions, enforce conservative obstacle recovery, and ensure only one controllable is enabled per state."
